{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A solemn rest, a remembrance of teru'ah.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Rosh HaShanah 29a): it is written (Numbers 29:1) ״יוֹם תְּרוּעָה יִהְיֶה לָכֶם״, and it is written ״זִכְרוֹן תְּרוּעָה״ — the one refers to a weekday, the other to the Sabbath; therefore it says ״שַׁבָּתוֹן זִכְרוֹן תְּרוּעָה״. And the distinction between Sabbath and weekday applies specifically in the provinces, but not in the Temple. A proof for the matter: from the fact that it is written in the passage of Pinchas, ״יוֹם תְּרוּעָה יִהְיֶה לָכֶם, וַעֲשִׂיתֶם עוֹלָה״ etc. — infer from this that it speaks of a place where the offerings are sacrificed, that is, in the Temple, where the Sabbath is set aside before the offerings, and then it is also set aside before the shofar. But here it says ״זִכְרוֹן תְּרוּעָה מִקְרָא קֹדֶשׁ כָּל מְלֶאכֶת עֲבוֹדָה לֹא תַעֲשׂוּ וְהִקְרַבְתֶּם״ etc. — since it distances the statement ״וְהִקְרַבְתֶּם״ and places the prohibition of labor adjacent to ״זִכְרוֹן תְּרוּעָה״, infer from this that it speaks of the provinces, where only the prohibition of labor applies and there are no offerings there. And we may say further that there is a distinction between ״וַעֲשִׂיתֶם״ and ״וְהִקְרַבְתֶּם״, for עֲשִׂיָּה means actual action, and that is in the Temple; but הַקְרָבָה applies also to the remembrance of the offerings in prayer, for through them Israel draw near to HaShem — and that is in the provinces."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:38:13.120802663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}